    {
        "content": "<p>Given all of the chatter of program verification in Lean, I figured now is a good time send an update to this thread. Thanks to the hard work of many contributors, Iris-Lean is now capable of formalizing some pretty serious Iris program logics! </p>\n<p>Recently I asked my robot to help me port <a href=\"https://iris-project.org/pdfs/2025-popl-approxis.pdf\">Approxis</a> from Rocq to Lean. To give you an idea of the scope: Approxis is a relational separation logic for a deeply-embedded functional language, which includes features like higher-order state and probabilistic choice.  The logic uses Iris constructions like invariants and ReLoC style spec programs, connected to the IProp model by the same extensible typeclass machinery as Rocq. The basic Approxis adequacy theorem proves the existence of an approximate probabilistic coupling between two limit executions of a program, which I formalized in terms of Mathlib's probability spaces. The Iris proofs take place in a port of the Iris proofmode. </p>\n<p>This adequacy theorem for Approxis is sorry-free. Of course there's still a lot of work between here and \"full Approxis\" (including de-LLMfying the codebase--the robot managed to get way further than I expected!). If nothing else, hopefully this theorem demonstrates that Iris-Lean is in a state suitable to start exploring more serious program logic problems. </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp_adequacy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">GF</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BundledGFunctors</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IPre</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AppPreGS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GF</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ISPre</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SpecPreGS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GF</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IECPre</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ECPreGS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GF</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IInvPre</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">InvGpreS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GF</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Exp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">State</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ENNReal</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Hwp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ApproxisGS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GF</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢@</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">IProp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GF</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iprop</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⤇</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iprop</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Val</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⤇</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Exp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofVal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⌜</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v'</span><span class=\"bp\">⌝</span><span class=\"o\">))))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">AddCoupl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">adequacyRel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">limExec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"n\">expr</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">limExec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">e'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ'</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·.</span><span class=\"n\">expr</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>If you haven't checked it out in a while, please feel free to give Iris-Lean a shot! My collaborators and I have a ton of other interesting projects in the works. Feel free to let us know what you think in <a class=\"stream\" data-stream-id=\"490604\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean\">#iris-lean</a>!</p>",
